t platforms: Cortex should not rebuild generic agent runtime, cloud sandbox, model gateway, knowledge graph, CI, or formal/test tooling. It should test whether a small portable lifecycle/assurance controller adds measurable engineering reliability above those mature substrates.\n\nThe detailed handoff is intentionally stored in-repo so a new session can resume from GitHub without depending on the current chat transcript.\n\n## Locked direction recorded\n\n- Microsoft Agent Framework first as the local/MIT runtime substrate;\n- runtime-neutral Cortex semantics so AWS AgentCore can be qualified later without a lifecycle rewrite;\n- LiteLLM remains the model/provider boundary;\n- FOSSIL owns durable knowledge/provenance/lineage/KG, not active Cortex state;\n- project owns current requirements/current artifacts/acceptance meaning;\n- assurance methods remain external providers that return version-bound evidence;\n- GitHub/CI remains an independent merge/release boundary;\n- V6 must eventually beat a conventional coding-agent + CI/review baseline or be narrowed/killed.\n\n## Validation\n\nDocumentation-only change. Compared `main...agent/locked-plan-handoff`: four files changed, no source/runtime files modified. Issue #9 and child issues #10–#19 contain mechanical acceptance criteria for the new work packages.\n\nDocs-Impact: updated architecture, project charter, roadmap, and added the durable locked-plan handoff.\n","created_at":"2026-08-18T02:37:00Z","updated_at":"2026-08-18T02:38:39Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"3c582fa6fb05c3e3235c1b5107d3b9b444910d31","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":true,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pukujan/Cortex-v6/pulls/20/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pukujan/Cortex-v6/pulls/20/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Pukujan/Cortex-v6/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.g